t.children(f,[('Removing the upper endpoint from D removes this S witness.','The witness equals the removed endpoint.'),('Keeping the upper endpoint while removing1/2 preserves the joint witness.','Its value1 is still admitted and both predicates still hold.'),('A test restricted to interior probability values can miss this endpoint overlap.','S has no interior witness while its endpoint witness exists.')])
t.children(h,[('A single valid witness is sufficient for this existential answer.','Existential semantics require at least one, not a majority.'),('Adding p=1/4 to the domain cannot destroy the existing witness.','The expanded set still contains1 and predicates remain fixed.'),('Counting non-witnesses cannot overturn a verified existential witness.','Existence is not a vote across domain points.')])
t.children(i,[('A definition change could alter compatibility even if the source label stayed fixed.','Compatibility is computed from predicates; strict U versus positive M differs at1.'),('A label change could leave compatibility fixed if the predicates stayed fixed.','The held-fixed computation does not consume that label.'),('The author’s intended meaning remains a different unresolved question.','The root is a stipulated model, and no author-context premise has been added.')])
