a,b,c=t.children(1,[('A summary-only deterministic selector receives identical input in A andB.','Declared summary contains prior, payoffs, price and overall accuracy, all equal.'),('Act-now is optimal among buy/now in A, and buy is optimal in B.','FRQ42 exact net values are A:.8 versus1 and B:1.2 versus1.'),('The conditional observation distributions differ even though overall accuracy matches.','The root gives different sensitivity/specificity pairs.')])
d,e,f=t.children(a,[('A deterministic function of that identical summary returns the same choice in both models.','Equal inputs to a deterministic function have equal outputs.'),('Repeating the unchanged summary supplies no distinction between A andB.','Each repetition contains the same values.'),('The identical accuracy label alone does not identify the confusion matrix.','A andB are distinct matrices consistent with that label and prior.')])
g,h,i=t.children(d,[('That same buy/now output is suboptimal in at least one of A orB.','R3 establishes opposite strict optima; one common choice cannot equal both.'),('A fixed always-buy selector loses .2 relative to the optimum in A.','A buy=.8 while now=1.'),('A fixed always-now selector loses .2 relative to the optimum in B.','B now=1 while buy=1.2.')])
j,k,l=t.children(g,[('No deterministic selector restricted to that summary is optimal in both admitted models.','Any such selector has a common output, and the parent covers both possible actions.'),('Choosing a more confident label for the same output does not remove its .2 payoff deficit in the losing case.','Confidence label is not part of the fixed payoff calculation.'),('A claim of uniform optimality must therefore change an admitted condition or acquire a distinguishing input.','With model set, summary and criterion fixed, the parent contradiction remains.')])
m,n,o=t.children(j,[('Adding a new feature that is constant across A andB leaves the selector inputs identical.','Concatenating equal summary with an equal constant preserves equality.'),('An observed feature that identifies A versusB would remove this particular ambiguity.','The selector could choose the model’s known strict optimum from R3.'),('Relaxing uniform optimality to a regret objective changes the guarantee being requested.','The criterion no longer requires zero loss in each model.')])
